30e33c0f-b507-4c8d-a580-30ada1fcd9c0.result_summary:
# Summary of changes for run 13234482-9f15-466b-a8a2-9b721286fac2
Added a strictly bottom-up formalization of the Naslund–Sawin slice-rank bound for 3-sunflower-free families in `Catalog/Combinatorics/SliceRankSunflowerFree.lean` (module `Catalog.Combinatorics.SliceRankSunflowerFree`). The file compiles (verified) with no circular dependencies; every declaration is tagged with its layer and the more primitive results it uses.

Architecture:

Layer 0 — Definitions (all defined):
- `IsSlice`, `SliceRankLE` (slice rank of `X×X×X → 𝔽` as a length-bounded list of rank-one slices);
- `diagTensor`, `diagSupport` (diagonal tensor and its support);
- `SunflowerFree` (no three distinct members with equal pairwise intersections).

Layer 1 — Basic properties:
- `sliceRankLE_zero`, `SliceRankLE.mono`, `sliceRankLE_add` (subadditivity) — proved;
- `diagTensor_support_card_le_sliceRank` (the Slice Rank Lemma, Tao 2016) — stated correctly and left as `sorry`; it is the core linear-algebra fact and does not reference any sunflower bound.

Layer 2 — The Naslund–Sawin construction over 𝔽₃ = ZMod 3:
- `ind`, `TFcore` (per-coordinate factor `1 - (aᵢbᵢ + bᵢcᵢ + cᵢaᵢ)`), `TF`, `famDiag`;
- `ind_sq`, `TFcore_diag` (the tensor is `1` on the diagonal), `diagSupport_famDiag` — proved;
- `TF_offdiagonal_zero` — proved: on a sunflower-free uniform (hence antichain) family the tensor vanishes off the diagonal (the combinatorial heart: some coordinate lies in exactly two of the three sets);
- `TF_eq_diagTensor` — proved: under those hypotheses `TF 𝓕` equals the diagonal tensor with support `𝓕`;
- `Mbound` (Croot–Lev–Pach squarefree-monomial count of degree ≤ n/3) and `TF_sliceRank_le` (polynomial slice-rank bound) — the latter left as `sorry`.

Layer 3 — Main results (referencing only Layers 1–2):
- `sunflowerFree_uniform_bound` — proved: a uniform sunflower-free family has size ≤ `3·Mbound n`;
- `SunflowerFree.subset`, `sunflowerFree_bound` — proved: an arbitrary sunflower-free family has size ≤ `(n+1)·3·Mbound n` (pigeonhole over the n+1 cardinality slabs);
- `Mbound_asymptotic` (entropy bound `Mbound n ≤ K·(3/2^{2/3})ⁿ`) — left as `sorry`;
- `sunflowerFree_bound_asymptotic` — proved from the two preceding results: `#𝓕 ≤ K·(n+1)·(3/2^{2/3})ⁿ`, the Naslund–Sawin exponential rate `3/2^{2/3} ≈ 1.89`.

Notes on faithfulness: the abstract diagonal-tensor Slice Rank Lemma is stated in its exact form (`#S ≤ r`) rather than the garbled `|S| ≤ 3qr²` in the brief; the exponential base `3/2^{2/3}` follows the `n/3` degree threshold. The honest polynomial factor obtained here is `n+1` (from the crude cardinality-slab pigeonhole); the sharper `n^{1/6}` factor from Naslund–Sawin's degree optimization is a strictly stronger statement and is documented in the docstring rather than asserted, to avoid stating an unverified bound.

Only three `sorry`s remain, all on the genuinely hard mathematical cores (the Slice Rank Lemma, the Croot–Lev–Pach polynomial bound, and the binomial entropy asymptotic), consistent with the requested `sorry_fill` mode. No axioms or `@[implemented_by]` were introduced. All work is committed and pushed.

